<!--
    kuna strict fix (P3, cleanup pool, RuleExpandLoad; no option).

    A LOAD narrower than its pointer's pointee printed as a read of the whole
    field or element, truncated or masked: `(uint2)p[1]` for the two bytes at
    p + 4, `(q[1] & 0x30) != 0x10` for the byte at q + 8.  Compiled, those read
    four and eight bytes where the program reads two and one, and fault when
    the object ends at the last byte the program reads, at the end of a page.
    A narrow read now prints at its own width and offset.  The AND-compare form
    stays only inside a field of a declared record, where the whole field
    exists and the compare can use the field's own constants.

    gcc -O2 of (struct rec { char *name; unsigned flags; unsigned short tag;
    unsigned short pad; long id; }):

      t_low: movzx eax,word [rdi+8] / ret          *(unsigned short *)&r->flags
      t_bit: movzx eax,byte [rdi+9] / and eax,0x30 / cmp al,0x10 / je sink(7)
      p_low: movzx eax,word [rdi+4] / ret          through unsigned *p
      p_bit: movzx eax,word [rdi+4] / and ax,0x300 / cmp ax,0x100 / je sink(7)
      q_bit: movzx eax,byte [rdi+8] / and eax,0x30 / cmp al,0x10 / je sink(7)
      s_set: [mov qword [rdi+8],3] / mov byte [rdi+9],dl   (a narrow store)

    One pass, defaults only: t_low, p_low, p_bit and q_bit read at their own
    width, t_bit keeps the whole-field compare of the declared record, and the
    store stays one byte wide.
-->
